NOT a backport - this fix does not exist upstream. Companion to 0003: same function, same
reason, a different unencodable term.

`dev_lua:do_encode/2` recurses through maps and lists and passes anything else through to
`luerl:encode/2`, whose final clause is `error({badarg, Term})`. A CACHE LINK - `{link, ID,
#{<<"lazy">> => false, <<"type">> => <<"link">>}}` - is such a term, and links appear in
practically every message a hook is asked to price.

The `hb_cache:ensure_all_loaded/2` calls already in the map and list clauses do NOT cover it,
which is the part that is easy to get wrong. They run on the ALREADY-CONVERTED `[{Key, Value}]`
proplist, and `ensure_all_loaded/3`'s list clause numbers the list and recurses per ELEMENT - so
each element is the whole `{Key, Value}` tuple, which is not a link, and its value is never
looked at. Every map converted to a proplist therefore keeps its links, and every message is
such a map.

WHAT IT COST US. Self-hosted bundling was enabled on stage and live on 2026-08-27 by config
alone and publishing stopped dead. The node posts each scheduled message and assignment to its
own `~bundler@1.0/tx`; that POST runs the `on/request` hooks, p4 asks the Lua write-gate to
price it, the request fails to ENCODE, and `dev_p4` reports "Could not estimate price of
request." (HTTP 400). `dev_scheduler_server` DISCARDS the upload result
(`dev_scheduler_server.erl:266-269`), so the refusal is dropped and never retried: slots keep
advancing and their assignments never reach Arweave. Eight stage slots were lost that way before
it was reverted. Dev was unaffected only because its pricing device is `faff@1.0`, a built-in
that never encodes anything into Lua.

⚠️ It is NOT the write-gate's `n == 0 -> REFUSE` rule, which was the obvious suspect and the
wrong one. Verified by substitution: a gate whose `estimate` returns ADMIT unconditionally fails
identically, and the UNMODIFIED gate admits the upload once this patch is in. The gate needs no
change and was not changed.

Loading the link where it is found, rather than reordering the `ensure_all_loaded` calls, keeps
the existing traversal intact and costs nothing for a message with no links. A link encodes as
the value it points at, so a script sees an ordinary value.

Deliberately narrow, for the reason 0003 records: a general "render any unencodable tuple"
fallback turns the `{error, {device_not_loadable, _}}` of a `device-sandbox` denial into a
string the script reads and returns. `ao_core_sandbox_test` asserts that denial stays an error.

VALIDATED on this image (edge @ 14e9f68a + 0002 + 0003): upstream `dev_lua` 22/22 and `dev_p4`
3/3 pass with the clause in place, and on a locally gated node the write-gate as deployed admits
the node's own upload - message and assignment both reach the bundler - while an unsigned
chargeable request and a stranger's write are still refused. Reproduce with anyone-protocol
`smart-contracts/ao/scripts/probe/gated-bundler-repro.ts`.

diff --git a/src/preloaded/vm/dev_lua.erl b/src/preloaded/vm/dev_lua.erl
